    "notOk": [
      "the defaults are 240 s for every adapter call and 180 s for one PowerShell start, and the shell bound is the smaller one",
      "one knob drives both bounds: the shell bound is 75 percent of the outer bound, an explicit shell bound may only be smaller",
      "the environment variable QUALIFY_TIMEOUT_MS sets the same two bounds, an option wins over it, and the name is case-insensitive",
      "a value that is not an integer number of milliseconds from 1 to 1800000 is refused by name, never guessed",
      "an invalid timeout is a typed failure before anything is asked, and no timeout ever makes a check pass",
      "the option shortens both waits: a hung shell is ended at 75 percent of the outer bound and both answers time out",
      "an explicit shell bound below the outer bound is kept, one above it is clamped so that the outer bound never fires first",
      "the environment variable reaches the PowerShell bound through qualifyEdge()",
      "the command line has one flag, --timeout-ms <n>, that is validated and handed to the check and to the requalification"
    ]
